# Localization

When you add or change user-facing text in the app, update `Droword/Localizable.xcstrings` in the same turn. Do not leave English-only keys.

## Locales

Translate every new or edited key into all of these (same set as existing strings):

`en`, `ru`, `de`, `es`, `fr`, `it`, `pt-PT`, `ja`, `ko`, `ar`, `zh-Hans`, `zh-Hant`

Use real native wording, not literal word-for-word English. Match the tone of nearby strings (friendly tutor, short UI labels).

## Plurals and number

If the string depends on a count (`%lld`, `%d`, “N words”, days, badges, etc.):

- Use String Catalog `variations.plural` for every locale.
- Fill the categories that language needs (`one` / `other` minimum; also `zero` / `few` / `many` / `two` when Russian, Arabic, etc. require them).
- Decline nouns and adjectives correctly (Russian: 1 слово / 2 слова / 5 слов; Arabic dual/plural; etc.).
- Prefer `String(localized:defaultValue:)` / interpolated localized strings that pick plural forms automatically.

Look at existing plural keys in `Localizable.xcstrings` (e.g. `"%lld new words"`) and mirror that shape.

## Line breaks and non-breaking spaces

UI labels wrap by spaces. Avoid orphan letters and ugly mid-phrase breaks:

- Put a **non-breaking space** (`\u{00A0}`, NBSP) between words that must stay on one line: number + unit (`7\u{00A0}días`, `%lld\u{00A0}words`), short title pairs (`Font\u{00A0}size`, `Efectos\u{00A0}estacionales`), name + short word (`App\u{00A0}customization`).
- Prefer a shorter translation for narrow trailing values (On/Off → `Sí`/`No`, `Вкл`/`Выкл`) instead of long words that wrap to a single letter (`Desactivad` / `o`).
- Compact chrome buttons (`Done`, `Select`, `Skip`, `Finish`, `Got it`, chip CTAs): keep labels short in every locale. Prefer `OK` / `Listo` / `Fatto` / `Fertig` / `Готово` over long forms like French `Terminé` or German `Überspringen` when the control is a small chip.
- On settings rows with a trailing value, keep `lineLimit(1)` (and light `minimumScaleFactor` if needed) on the value; let the title wrap or shrink first.
- Soft hyphen (`\u{00AD}`) only when a long single word must break mid-word on purpose — prefer shorter copy first.

In Swift string literals: `"Font\u{00A0}size"`. In the string catalog JSON the same Unicode character is fine.

## Do not

- Ship a new `Text("…")` / `LocalizedStringKey` without catalog entries for every locale.
- Reuse an old key whose English meaning changed without updating all locales.
- Skip plural variants and rely on English “word/words” only.
- Translate worker API prompts or code comments as product UI (UI only).
- Leave long On/Off-style labels that orphan one letter on the next line in Romance languages.

Share extension `.lproj` files: update them when the string is also shown in the Share extension.
